  <data name="OverviewArchitecture.[using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Automation]AutomationProperties.Name" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Requests can be made from Slack or Mattermost on another device, and Chat Agent Bridge on the running PC will receive them. After checking on your PC, run Codex CLI or Claude Code CLI and receive the checked and shared results in the same thread.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="chatAgentBridgeDesktopMainPageTextBlock007.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A request sent from a phone or browser through Slack or Mattermost reaches Chat Agent Bridge on your running PC. The bridge runs Codex CLI or Claude Code CLI in the selected project. Shared results return to the same thread. Where AI processing takes place depends on the CLI and AI service settings.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="chatAgentBridgeDesktopMainPageTextBlock008.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Choose the CLI, model, and working folder in Agent settings.
2. Save the chat credentials in Connection settings, then connect from Chat inbox.
3. Send a request from another device. In Mattermost, start with !cab or an @mention of the connected bot, followed by your request. In Slack, mention the bot or use !cab in a thread reply.
4. Review and approve the request on this PC, then review and share the result to return it to the same thread.

Keep this app and your local PC running to stay connected.</value>
  </data>
